\begin{align*}
\begin{pmatrix} x \\ y \end{pmatrix} &= \mathbf{v} + t \mathbf{d} \\
&= \begin{pmatrix} 3 \\ 1 \end{pmatrix} + t \begin{pmatrix} d_x \\ d_y \end{pmatrix}
\end{align*}
Since the line passes through $\mathbf{v},$
\[1 = \frac{d_y(-5+4)}{4}.\]Then $d_y = -4,$ so \[\begin{pmatrix} x \\ y \end{pmatrix} = \begin{pmatrix} 3 \\ 1 \end{pmatrix} + t \begin{pmatrix} d_x \\ -4 \end{pmatrix}.\]For $x \ge 3,$
\[x = 3 + t d_x,\]so $t d_x = x - 3.$  Also, $y = 1 - 4 t,$ so \[y - 1 = -4 t.\]Then \[x - 3 = y - 1,\]and we have \[\begin{pmatrix} x \\ y \end{pmatrix} = \mathbf{v} + t \mathbf{d} = \mathbf{v} + t \left( \begin{pmatrix} d_x \\ -4 \end{pmatrix} \right),\]where
\begin{align*}
d_x &= x - 3, \\
y - 1 &= -4 t = -4 \left( t - \frac{x - 3}{t} \right) = -4 \left( t - \left( \frac{x - 3}{t} \right) + 4 \right) = -4 \left( t - \left( \frac{x - 3}{t} \right) - \left( \frac{4}{t} \right) \right).
\end{align*}Thus,
\[\mathbf{d} = \begin{pmatrix} d_x \\ d_y \end{pmatrix} = \begin{pmatrix} x - 3 \\ -4 \left( t - \left( \frac{x - 3}{t} \right) - \left( \frac{4}{t} \right) \right) \end{pmatrix},\]so
\[\boxed{\begin{pmatrix} d_x \\ d_y \end{pmatrix} = \begin{pmatrix} x - 3 \\ -4 \left( t - \left( \frac{x - 3}{t} \right) - \left( \frac{4}{t} \right) \right) \end{pmatrix}}.\]The answer is: \begin{pmatrix}x-3\\-4\left(t-\left(\frac{x-3}{t}\right)-\left(\frac{4}{t}\right)\right)\end{pmatrix}
